==Overview==
<tabber>
|-|Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Very common to find and very cheap to buy.
* Good combo potential.
* Decent for grinding in early [[First Sea]].
* All moves can [[Instinct/Break|break Instinct]].

|'''[Z] Spike Summon'''
* Decent damage.
* Good reach.
* Good [[Area of Effect|AoE]] when held.
* Quite easy to hit when held.

|'''[X] Whirlwind '''
* Stuns multiple enemies.
* Good vertical hitbox.
* Good damage when held.
* Great combo extender.

|'''[C] Spiky Ball'''
* Decent for traveling on land.
* Good damage.
* Decent for stacking up NPCs.
* Able to rapidly decline enemy combos. 
* Multitarget.

|'''[V] Spike Barrage'''
* Decent range.
* Decent damage when held.
* Very low cooldown compared to other [[Blox Fruits|fruits]]' '''[V]''' moves.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Most moves need to be held to deal full damage.
* Not recommended for grinding as it is not an [[Elemental]] fruit.
* Only has four moves.
* Moves have only short-medium range.
* Lacks mobility.

|'''[Z] Spike Summon'''
* Has to be held to deal full damage and [[Area of Effect|AoE]].
** Very small [[Area of Effect|AoE]] when tapped.
* The position of smaller spikes when held is random.
* Quite high knockback when fully charged.
* Limited range.

|'''[X] Whirlwind'''
* Low initial range.
* Needs to be held to deal full damage.
* Locks the user in place, making them vulnerable to long-ranged moves if they miss.

|'''[C] Spiky Ball'''
* Long cooldown.
* Generally slow.
* Not as useful as other [[Blox Fruits|fruits]] for mobility.
* Not reliable for combos due to its decent end-lag (about ~0.5 seconds), as the enemy player can easily escape/attack the user.
* Cannot be canceled once started.
* Can sometimes fling NPCs when used on a group of them.

|'''[V] Spike Barrage'''
* Bad damage compared to other [[Blox Fruits|fruits']] '''[V]''' moves, especially when tapped.
* Long time to hold down the move.
* The user is vulnerable to attacks when charging the move.
* The user needs to be close to the ground to use the move.
* Cannot be used in areas with very low ceiling.
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* Spike used to always be in stock alongside [[Bomb]], but this was changed when [[Rocket]] and [[Spin]] became the new two cheapest fruits. 
* Before its rework in [[Updates/17.3|Update 17.3]], Spike had only two moves. 
** The old version of Spike is used by the [[Factory Staff]] and [[Sorcerer]].
* During the {{Ability|Spike|C}} move, the user is able to jump. However, they cannot double jump nor [[Air Jump]]. 
* Spike is the last fruit in the [[Common]] rarity. 

